  "content": "{\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"No positive integer start exists.\",\n      \"justification\": \"Let n1 be the first odd value and n2 the next. Exact exponents k1=1 and k2=2 require 2n2=3n1+1 and 4n1=3n2+1. Eliminating n2 gives 8n1=9n1+5, equivalently (2^(1+2)-9)n1=3+2^1, so n1=-5. Therefore the cycle equation has no positive integer solution.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"claim_status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n  \"first_missing_step\": null,\n  \"unexpected_findings\": []\n}",
